# Code Comments

Always include comments on any code that is not obviously self explanatory. Keep them short and meaningful. Information density is key.

Code comments should succinctly denote the purpose or what is being accomplished by the code, not just paraphrasing the code operations themselves.

Commenting code explains the history of the thought process behind the code, making it easier for humans to read, and for AI agents to build upon.
